note The unit a step is pinned with. An anchor is a slice of lines in one file, but it is stored relative to the start of the enclosing symbol, so code moving above it does not break it; only the anchored text changing does, and a stored hash is how that is detected. This is the whole mechanism behind stale steps and behind coverage: an anchor that resolves cleanly marks its symbol covered, one that does not is red everywhere and has to be re-pinned by whoever changed the code.

